This is a project focused on XAI of BERT like models in HSD in portuguese. Right now we are trying to expand the project and make more robust for a scientific publication. Your first task is to help me change the Cross Validation we were doing, at  @file:src\classify.py  in a function called fineTune: it needs to use StratifiedKFold instead of KFold, we need to be able to use this function for a baseline model and a traditional model like an SVM as well as the BERT models, we need to calculate the accuracy, f1-micro, f1-macro, precision and recall of the whole thing and per class, and make sure that all of the models use the same fold distribution.
Looking at the changes you made, there are some things I would would like to point out that I think need to be fixed (you can evaluate them further and say if you think they are valid remarks and should be made or not): I think we are leaking data for the bert models the way the code is structured right now, we need to reinitialize the models with a fresh new model every single fold; And there are some inconsistencies like we extract labels and text differently for SVM and Baseline, and the way we are saving the models, we save only the model from the last fold, we should either save all the models or not save any of them and only look at the final results. One other thing I would like you to do separetely is create a new stratification function (don't touch the one you did already) where you stratify it by class and not multilabel combinations. Don't assume things, if anything is unclear ask me.
For reinitializing the BERT model each fold, if we add this reset() method, can we be sure there would be no data leakage anymore? As for the stratification function, can you explain a bit more about the iterative stratification?
Now I think you can proceed with your plan to eliminate those inconsistencies, create the reset() module for reinstanciating the bert model and use IterativeStratification on the new function.
